- Solar Hyperscaler (will_said): low-power solar nodes to out-compete AWS for compute/storage. Verified: literal 1-panel-1-node NOT viable (~514 Wh/day December panel vs 600–960 Wh/day for Starlink Mini alone); workable form is a pooled farm-site pod (shared panels/battery, duty-cycled Starlink, data by physical shuttle; drones deferred, FAA BVLOS). Classification: research / option ticket, not a business.
- Solar correction (will_said): entirely off-grid — marginal energy cost zero, no interconnect cost; at AWS list rates, cashflow positive within months after hardware. Verified: holds as monthly-cashflow claim, refuted as payback claim for Model A. Timing (will_said): not pushed at current prices; sells itself ~2028–2029. Homelab proof (verified): encrypted backup vault for SMBs via Duey's book ($49/site/month vs ~$7 cost, ~86% margin); day-10 gate: Duey names ≥3 candidates or the channel is not real. Storage carries the model; batch inference fails on cash.
