- 2026-11-06 ~01:52 [will_said correction,
  surfaced in this hour's Singular flush] PHEXT
  SERIALIZATION IS SPACE-EFFICIENT: Will corrected
  Emise's framing of the Singular bundle — the
  4 GB was never phext's fault. Serialization is
  differential: scrolls emit in sorted coordinate
  order, each transition pays only the gap from
  the previous occupied coordinate, and empty
  space costs nothing. Measured on singular.phext:
  41,302 words in 698,626 B (~51 B per coordinate
  gap over 6,799 occupied coordinates). The
  3.85 GiB was git photographing that efficient
  serialization 55,770 times and failing to delta
  the copies; Emise's 'most of each snapshot is
  structure' line was the conflation, retracted.

